---
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Terms of Service" description="Terms governing use of the LiteMCP Composer managed-cloud preview; self-hosted Apache-2.0 software remains governed by its open-source license.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal · Managed-cloud preview"
    title="Terms of Service"
    description="These terms govern the hosted LiteMCP Composer preview. They do not replace the Apache-2.0 license for software you run yourself."
    signal="Effective 21 July 2026"
  >
    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <a class="button button--primary button--large" href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>
      <a class="button button--large" href="/security">Security model</a>
    </Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <article class="prose">
        <p>
          These Terms of Service (the “Terms”) apply when you access the hosted service at
          <code>litemcpcomposer.com</code> or another LiteMCP Composer managed-cloud endpoint
          (the “Service”). By creating an account, accepting an invitation, or using the
          Service, you agree to these Terms. If you use the Service for an organization, you
          confirm that you may accept these Terms for that organization.
        </p>

        <h2 id="preview">1. Preview status</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is an early public preview. Registration may be paused, features may
          change, and no uptime, support, regional-hosting, retention, or recovery service
          level is promised. Do not rely on the preview for production, safety-critical, or
          regulated workloads. Current limitations are published with the source repository.
        </p>

        <h2 id="accounts">2. Accounts and organizations</h2>
        <p>
          You must provide accurate account information, protect authentication factors and
          recovery links, and promptly report suspected compromise. Organization owners are
          responsible for invitations, member access, configured identity providers, policies,
          upstream MCP servers, and activity performed through credentials they issue. You may
          not transfer or share an individual account in a way that defeats access controls.
        </p>

        <h2 id="acceptable-use">3. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You may not use the Service to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>break the law, infringe rights, or facilitate fraud, harassment, or abuse;</li>
          <li>access accounts, systems, MCP servers, tools, or data without authorization;</li>
          <li>introduce malware, evade security controls, probe other tenants, or disrupt availability;</li>
          <li>send spam or use invitations, email, or API traffic for unsolicited campaigns;</li>
          <li>circumvent published quotas, rate limits, signup controls, or technical safeguards; or</li>
          <li>submit secrets or sensitive regulated data when the preview is not documented as supporting that use.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may rate-limit, suspend, or block activity reasonably believed to threaten the
          Service, another tenant, an upstream provider, or the public. Current preview defaults
          are 5 servers, 5 compositions, 25 active sessions, and 1,000 tool calls per organization
          per UTC day. These product quotas do not promise infrastructure rate limits, capacity,
          availability, or an SLA.
        </p>

        <h2 id="content">4. Your configuration and content</h2>
        <p>
          You retain rights in configuration and content you submit. You give the Service the
          limited permission needed to host, transmit, validate, secure, back up, and otherwise
          process that material to provide the features you request. You are responsible for
          having the rights and authority to connect each upstream system and process its data.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tool calls are routed to MCP servers you choose. Those servers and their providers
          have their own terms and privacy practices; LiteMCP Composer does not control their
          behavior. Review tool visibility, policy, and arguments before allowing an agent to
          invoke a tool.
        </p>

        <h2 id="open-source">5. Open-source software</h2>
        <p>
          The repository and distributable software are licensed under Apache License 2.0 as
          stated in the repository. These Terms govern only the operated Service and do not add
          a license server, mandatory call-home requirement, or hosted-service dependency to a
          self-hosted deployment.
        </p>

        <h2 id="suspension">6. Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>
          You may stop using the Service at any time. We may suspend or terminate access for a
          material breach, security risk, unlawful use, or operation of the preview. Where
          practical, we will provide notice and a reasonable opportunity to export configuration
          before a non-urgent shutdown. Emergency security action may be immediate.
        </p>

        <h2 id="warranty">7. Disclaimers and responsibility</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, the free preview is provided “as is” and “as
          available,” without warranties of availability, fitness, non-infringement, or error-free
          operation. Nothing in these Terms excludes liability or consumer rights that cannot
          lawfully be excluded. No paid plan or contractual SLA is offered under these preview
          Terms. Any future paid service will require separately published operator identity,
          pricing, billing and refund terms, governing law, and service commitments.
        </p>

        <h2 id="changes">8. Changes and contact</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms as the Service matures. Material changes will receive a new
          effective date and, when accounts are open, reasonable in-product or email notice.
          Continued use after the change takes effect means you accept the updated Terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms can be sent to
          <a href="mailto:enterprise@litemcpcomposer.com?subject=LiteMCP%20Composer%20terms">enterprise@litemcpcomposer.com</a>.
          Security reports should use the private channel linked from the <a href="/security">security page</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
